<title>CHILE: Chile January copper exports rise to $608.2 mln.</title>
<headline>Chile January copper exports rise to $608.2 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's copper exports rose to $608.2 million last month from $479.9 a year ago, despite a seven percent fall in copper prices, said the Central Bank in its monthly report.</p>
<p>The increase reflects the rise in copper production as a result of new mines like Canadian-owned Quedrada Blanca coming into full production and expansion projects at existing pits including the giant Escondida mine.</p>
<p>Here are details of Chile's mining exports in January.</p>
<p> METAL			  Jan 1997	    Jan 1996</p>
<p> Copper			  608.2		 479.9</p>
<p> Iron			     18.0		  12.7</p>
<p> Salitre and iodine	   20.9		  20.9</p>
<p> Silver			   11.9		  12.0</p>
<p> Molybdenum		     19.3		  26.0</p>
<p> Lithium carbonate	     2.7		   3.0</p>
<p> Metallic gold and dore     43.7		  48.1</p>
<p> Gold mineral		    9.4		   9.5</p>
<p> Others			    8.6		   3.7</p>
<p> TOTAL			   742.7		 615.8</p>
<p>NOTE: All figures are in millions of dollars.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
</text>
